-Second-order dual-time stepping is used with $\Delta t=10^{-3}$.
-Forces are pressure-only, with unit reference area and chord and a pitching-moment reference at $x/c=0.25$.
-Because the exact steady inviscid drag is zero, $C_D$ is interpreted as a numerical-dissipation diagnostic rather than as a physical drag prediction.
