-Mesh $A$ contains 16,255 nodes and 32,077 triangles; mesh $B$ contains 22,508 nodes and 44,583 triangles.
-The independently converged steady states are denoted by $U_A^\star$ and $U_B^\star$, and every transferred calculation is compared with a native trajectory advanced on mesh $B$.
-For one transfer operator,
-\begin{equation}
